      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Examining the screenshot you posted, there are some issues in that script that we can not trace back to issues in the VRChat client:\n\n- It tries to spawn from the pool without verifying that it has ownership over the pool itself\n\n- It tries to set ownership of the resulting object without verifying that it received an object (this can fail)\n\n- It doesn't account for the fact that all clients are running OnPlayerJoined, but you'd only want one to actually spawn the object\n\n- Your `OnOwnershipTransferred` callback is on the script that is managing the pool, and not on the object that is being spawned from the pool - so it would only be called for when the pool gets transferred, not the spawned objects\n\nYou mentioned ownership requests in the comment, but it is unclear what the expectation there is.\n\nWith that in mind, do you have a specific scenario where you'd expect the client to behave differently, or found a mismatch with our documentation on https://creators.vrchat.com ?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
